# Workflow

- Read the project, architecture, active roadmap phase, and relevant feature
  documentation before changing code.
- Inspect existing code before proposing new structure.
- Implement only the requested feature within the active phase.
- Finish one coherent vertical slice, including appropriate tests and docs,
  before starting another.
- Prefer the simplest correct solution that preserves existing module
  boundaries.
- Do not add future features, speculative abstractions, unrelated refactors,
  dependencies, tables, endpoints, or infrastructure.
- Record valuable future ideas in the backlog rather than implementing them.
- Ask for clarification only when a missing decision materially changes scope,
  data, security, or user behavior.
- Keep changes focused and run checks proportional to their risk.
- Update canonical documentation when behavior, architecture, schema, API, or
  roadmap status changes.
